Make AppealMate deployable on Vercel

Adds a WSGI adapter (api/index.py) serving the same endpoints as server.py,
plus vercel.json routing. Two changes were required to work on a serverless
host:

- store.py now resolves the SQLite path at runtime. Vercel mounts the project
  read-only, so the database goes to /tmp there and stays beside the source
  locally.
- Sessions are persisted in the database instead of an in-memory dict, since
  each request may be a fresh invocation with no shared memory.

verify_vercel_adapter.py exercises all 15 routes through the adapter under
wsgiref, so the serverless path is tested locally rather than assumed.
